{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/635284-fan-made-pantheon-the-great-old-ones-cthulhu-mythos","id":635284,"title":"[Fan-Made Pantheon] The Great Old Ones (Cthulhu Mythos)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-21T18:11:49-07:00","id":635284,"title":"[Fan-Made Pantheon] The Great Old Ones (Cthulhu Mythos)","content":"Well, it's finally over. I hoped to post this on Lovecraft's birthday but of course I had to catch a fever.<br /> <br /> Hello everybody. Six years or more ago, under the name of Atomic Hermit, I began writing a pantheon based on the creation of H.P. Lovecraft. With the help of some other forumites, I kept writing for a couple of months but then I began the university and I could not find enough time to complete my work. I left it in a pen drive with the intention to finish it but never got around doing that. I recently found that pen drive and the intention resurfaced but it was the message of another member of the forum who wondered what happened to my work that really persuaded me getting back to it.<br /> <br /> Now that I'm almost done with my studies and blessed with some free time, I took a brief pause, spent a couple of weeks writing and now I've finished. For all those who waited this for so long, I apologize. Sorry, life's gets in the way and the last few years were quite turbolent for me. I sincerely hope that what I've done will satisfy you. For all the others, I hope you'll enjoy what I wrote as well.<br /> <br /> I could say more, but most of it is covered in the Introduction Chapter. Please take some moments to read it.<br /> <br /> There's a chapter at the end called Storytelling. It's empty for a reason: while I have a few things in mind that could probably deserve being pointed out when using the Great Old Ones in Scion and roleplaying a Scion of Cthulhu, I prefer to see what points arise from the discussion so I can write the chapter in a coherent way. If no discussion happens, well, I'll write what I planned to do in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Any criticism of comments you want to make is really appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 09-07-2021, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T19:36:19-07:00","id":635326,"title":"","content":"Haven't finished reading through what you've uploaded, and all of my knowledge on the works of Lovecraft come from the Tale of Old Man Henderson (such an amusing tale) and the Pathfinder Bestiary 4, but so far I am interested. If I were a player in a game that allowed these guys I'd definitely be maxing out the PPS for a GOO Scion (and notably eventually looking like the D2 version of the title character for the Diablo franchise)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T05:18:01-07:00","id":638959,"title":"","content":"This should help you out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ob7PfxvJCN0\" data-code=\"Ob7PfxvJCN0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ob7PfxvJCN0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T11:50:33-07:00","id":650347,"title":"","content":"Haven't finished reading all your work, but i just wanted to say well done. In my group there's one Yog Sothoth daughter, and she is delighted with the detail and work you've put into this. We played also with the idea of the Great Old Ones, but taking them not as Gods, but Titans. <br /> <br /> In our setting they are some sort of Primordial Titans, the embodiment of the Unknown Spheres. They set the universe in motion, creating entire dimensions and multiverses, most of them alien,dangerous and unimaginable to the human mind and soul. They set rules for each universe, and in this way, their orders became the Titans we know. Exhausted after having spent so much of their power,they went to sleep, and the World came to be as we know it. But something has happened, and now they are rising in their sleep, their consciouness slowly awakening. Their ways are slowly infecting the remaining Titans, warping them enough to set them free of their ancestral prisons. These new titans are utterly anathema to the Gods and their spawn, warping them and twisting them like they did with the Titans. The difference is that the Titans were the Great Old Ones servants. The Gods are just lowly, expendable spawn, and they will be fought and erased. And so it all begins. <br /> <br /> Aaaanyway, as my friend, i want to compliment you on your job. I loved &quot;Logos&quot; and the asociation you do with Ma'at and the others,for example. Also, i love the way thisTitan is bound to be &quot;neutral&quot; in this new War. That new Touchstone, The Lost City? Awesome. All in all, well done! <br /> <br /> I've still to read the Special Power, when i finish it all i will write again.<br /> <br /> PS. &quot;R.C.&quot; rules. And his silver key even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T07:38:28-07:00","id":651169,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the kind words. It took plenty of time, research and tinkering with the setting, but knowing that other Scion and Lovecraft's fans like my work really means a lot. I did some weird choices along the way but overall I'm proud of the results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/635284-fan-made-pantheon-the-great-old-ones-cthulhu-mythos?p=650347#post650347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our setting they are some sort of Primordial Titans, the embodiment of the Unknown Spheres. They set the universe in motion, creating entire dimensions and multiverses, most of them alien,dangerous and unimaginable to the human mind and soul. They set rules for each universe, and in this way, their orders became the Titans we know. Exhausted after having spent so much of their power,they went to sleep, and the World came to be as we know it. But something has happened, and now they are rising in their sleep, their consciouness slowly awakening. Their ways are slowly infecting the remaining Titans, warping them enough to set them free of their ancestral prisons. These new titans are utterly anathema to the Gods and their spawn, warping them and twisting them like they did with the Titans. The difference is that the Titans were the Great Old Ones servants. The Gods are just lowly, expendable spawn, and they will be fought and erased. And so it all begins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. That sure is a smart way to feature them as Titans, instead of just dropping them in the Overworld War.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/635284-fan-made-pantheon-the-great-old-ones-cthulhu-mythos?p=650347#post650347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS. &quot;R.C.&quot; rules. And his silver key even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you've liked him and got the references. Along with Al-Azif he's one on my most experimental ideas and while I like him quite a bit I was not sure other people would appreciate him as well, especially if they figured out who he was meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T18:35:38-08:00","id":761909,"title":"","content":"I'll add something to the long-dead thread, mostly because I love taking a piss at old HP's...less modern attitudes.<br /> <br /> <b>Sedibans (Guide ***):</b><br /> <br /> Quote: &quot;<i>You. You are of the cousin race, but also of the star race. Why have you come? Speak quickly, and perhaps we will treat you as cousin and not star.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Evolution is a messy thing. Contrary to the popular image of it as outlined in <i>The Evolution of Man, </i>it is not a straight line of forms leading to an increasingly intelligent and humanoid being. In fact, it isn't even just survival of the fittest; even before a being has become so genetically distant from its original species that it no longer is capable of breeding with it, there are numerous sub-species that are still more than genetically similar enough to breed with each other, and indeed, said genetic exchange actually is part of what drives the new subspecies into a distinct species of its own, with its own ecological niche. Humanity is no different; while <i>homo sapiens </i>is pretty much the end-all be-all of the non-divine hominids these days, once there was an entire smorgasbord of different kinds of humans with their own unique quirks and appearances. While the pessimistic would say we killed them all for looking strange, in truth the real answer is proof that cynics aren't nearly as all-knowing as they fear; the many subspecies got along so well that their tribal groupings merged, and as children sprung from that union, it just turned out that the appearance and quirks of the <i>sapiens</i> subspecies is dominant (the vast majority of people with European ancestry have at least one Neanderthal in their family history, for example). That same interbreeding and hybridization wasn't something new to hairless apes; back when humans were just bipedal, unusually intelligent monkeys known collectively as australopiths. the subspecies bred easily and freely, powering their eventual loss of hair and ever greater intellect. In fact, most anthropologists believe that, before they went extinct, early hominids had children with the remaining australopiths, ensuring their predecessors would live on through their descendants.<br /> <br /> These anthropologists are mostly right about that, except for two things: One, &quot;early&quot; can be dropped, and two, because it should really be in the present tense.<br /> <br /> Sedibans are the sole remaining species of australopith alive, a genetic quirk meaning the homo sapiens in their ancestry is actually recessive. Despite being far more histrute and somewhat more hunched than modern humans, they are actually just as intelligent, and can speak other languages perfectly fine, albeit with something of a lisp due to the shape of their teeth. Sedibans resemble man-sized, white- or grey-furred bonobos that prefer to walk upright, with a rather human face-mostly because, genetically and mentally speaking, they are human. Sedibans are close enough to <i>homo sapiens </i>to produce fertile offspring with the help of some of their sorcery, at which point the hybrids are quite capable of having children with either race until the genetic drift fully reintegrates them into either subspecies. They actually evolved full sapience and souls first due to their less-than-effective natural camouflage forcing them to evolve the capacity to outwit predators. In another world, they might have been the dominant species, but a quirk of Fate caused them to attract the destructive attentions of the obscure Outer God Daoloth to their first real civilization-while he is not nearly as malevolent as much of his kind, Daoloth destroyed most of the Sedibans and sent their entire culture back to subsistence hunter-gatherers, and by the time they recovered in their Congolese Terra Incognita, hairless hominids had gotten too far of a head start and simply taken up too much room and resources for the Sedibans to rebuild. They made their peace with it-these days, while the subspecies is not precisely <i>thriving, </i>they are no longer on the verge of extinction, and are working up the bravery to reveal their existence to their far more numerous cousins after being rather soured on the notion due to chain of events when one of their princesses ran off with a merchant that ended with her mother's corpse being burned by racist Victorians unable to accept that a nobleman could sully the line with someone of such foreign heritage (okay, technically it was due to the fact that, when it comes down to it, Sedibans still look like giant monkeys, but burning such an earth-shattering find as the queen's corpse in the heyday of discovery? That kind of reaction was motivated by rich white idiots unable to accept the fact that humans are of African origins-actually why the discovery of australopiths upset many of those same rich white idiots).<br /> <br /> Sedibans are not, generally speaking, creatures of Legend, but their lingering memories of Daoloth and the relics of his passing have given them a certain empathy and tolerance for the hidden world; they are very inured to the more insanity-provoking truths and abilities of the Great Old Ones, and a Sediban with the inclination can easily become a witch, or more accurately a &quot;shadowed shaman&quot;. Like the shamans of tribal homo sapiens, a Sediban shaman walks a lonely and feared, but usually valued path; their name comes from the fact that they walk in the shadows of their still-standing city for lore of the Great Old Ones they can use to protect their people, while constantly also being shadowed by the temptation to use it for selfish and destructive ends. More importantly, shamans know the secret spells and arts by which Sedibans can disguise themselves as their cousins and walk the world outside their hidden homelands (which isn't nearly as much a culture shock as it may seem-Sedibans regularly import modern technology to help them survive the remaining monsters in the Terra Incognita and stories of what to expect out there with it), and to help them produce children with the sizable minority of homo sapiens tribesmen that dwell with them (although an inexperienced or incompetent shaman often ends up infusing Daoloth's power into the parents-to-be and creating deformed and/or mentally disturbed offspring, as one House of Jermyn discovered). And of course, many Sediban-Homo Sapiens hybrids lack the genes that produce their distinctive fur pelts, allowing them to pass as rather long-limbed but otherwise completely normal members of the cousin race.<br /> <br /> While Sedibans and Sediban hybrids aren't pacifists, they generally are concerned with their own problems, and thus not open to becoming Followers to some nosy Scion. However, they are very open to sharing what lore they can find in their ruined city and their own broad knowledge of the Great Old One as Guides in return for a regular tithe of food and tools to help their tribes. While they're open to anyone, Scions of the Great Old Ones are far more likely to know of the reclusive people, though, and thus it's most likely to be one of them who has a Sediban Guide. Most of these are going to be shamans who have gone a little too far into the shadows and secretly worship Daoloth and all of his siblings, but a Scion who shows a respect for humanity might gain a more normal (and more trustworthy) Sediban as a Guide. Said Guide is also likely to be a moral voice, constantly reminding the Scion that he's or she's only half-god, and it's Earth he or she lives on; if the Great Old Ones destroy it, will said Scion be able to live with themselves, knowing all the purely human people they know are gone?<br /> <br /> (if you want, I can make the last Jermyn as an example of a Sediban hybrid).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-10-2015, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T09:55:53-08:00","id":765623,"title":"","content":"sweeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T14:32:09-08:00","id":770295,"title":"","content":"Actually, now that I think about it, this doesn't sound like it would be all that good as a pantheon. The whole Cthulhu mythos is about the futility of man and how they are subject to forces so far beyond their comprehension that the universe would not even be aware of their passing if humanity were to die out tomorrow. Doesn't exactly fit with the theme of defending the world from the encroaching Titan spawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T05:39:15-08:00","id":816805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/635284-fan-made-pantheon-the-great-old-ones-cthulhu-mythos?p=770295#post770295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, now that I think about it, this doesn't sound like it would be all that good as a pantheon. The whole Cthulhu mythos is about the futility of man and how they are subject to forces so far beyond their comprehension that the universe would not even be aware of their passing if humanity were to die out tomorrow. Doesn't exactly fit with the theme of defending the world from the encroaching Titan spawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're not wrong. The way I see it (and the way I wrote it) is that the Great Old Ones are forced into conflict with the Titanspawn not because they want to defend mankind or the world, but because they're defending themselves. Losing the human race and other Pantheons would mean giving a foothold to the Titan forces from which they would then inevitably proceed to defeat the Outer Gods as well.<br /> <br /> Once free from the Titanspawn menace, the Great Old Ones would probably try to assert their dominance with no regards to humanity. Which brings us to one of the things that I think would be most interesting in a game about the Scion of the Great Old Ones: making them care. Being a Scion of the Outer Gods brings you not only in front of the question whether you should keep traces of your human nature within yourself as you ascend to eldritch godhood, but also that, if you are still attached to mankind, how you manage to conciliate this fact with your divine relatives. Even for Scion standards, the Outer Gods are unequivocally unsuitable at being good parents, especially from a human standpoint. And yet, being one of their Scions puts you in the best possible position to make them start to care about mankind, in a way or the other. On paper, this should be impossible, and my fellow Lovecraft's purists tremble at the mere thought, but if there's a game where you can at least try to accomplish such unconceivable feats, that's Scion.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Perhaps also Exalted, but this is not the right forum for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-26-2016, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:48:50-08:00","id":816874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/635284-fan-made-pantheon-the-great-old-ones-cthulhu-mythos?p=816805#post816805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you're not wrong. The way I see it (and the way I wrote it) is that the Great Old Ones are forced into conflict with the Titanspawn not because they want to defend mankind or the world, but because they're defending themselves. Losing the human race and other Pantheons would mean giving a foothold to the Titan forces from which they would then inevitably proceed to defeat the Outer Gods as well.<br /> <br /> Once free from the Titanspawn menace, the Great Old Ones would probably try to assert their dominance with no regards to humanity. Which brings us to one of the things that I think would be most interesting in a game about the Scion of the Great Old Ones: making them care. Being a Scion of the Outer Gods brings you not only in front of the question whether you should keep traces of your human nature within yourself as you ascend to eldritch godhood, but also that, if you are still attached to mankind, how you manage to conciliate this fact with your divine relatives. Even for Scion standards, the Outer Gods are unequivocally unsuitable at being good parents, especially from a human standpoint. And yet, being one of their Scions puts you in the best possible position to make them start to care about mankind, in a way or the other. On paper, this should be impossible, and my fellow Lovecraft's purists tremble at the mere thought, but if there's a game where you can at least try to accomplish such unconceivable feats, that's Scion.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Perhaps also Exalted, but this is not the right forum for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And then you play as Cartman befriending the master of R'lyeh. Although in the video I linked previously, it does explain some of the Old Gods are responsible for creating humans in the first place, so there is some potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:52:11-08:00","id":816878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/635284-fan-made-pantheon-the-great-old-ones-cthulhu-mythos?p=816874#post816874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> And then you play as Cartman befriending the master of R'lyeh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that's always an option. But I'd rather play as Kenny looking for answers from the dark cults. Or an high Legend Mintberry Crunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T07:49:30-08:00","id":836402,"title":"","content":"Either I just had a crazy 